    "reason": "While JMdict lists 'section' as a gloss for 局部 (kyokubu), its common usage in Japanese is much narrower than the general English 'section'. 局部 often refers to a specific, localized, or anatomical part (e.g., 'affected part of the body'), and can even mean 'private parts'. It is not a natural or general equivalent for 'section' in contexts like 'a section of a book', 'a section of a city', or 'a section of a company'. A general learner would find this translation misleading or inappropriate for most uses of 'section'.",
